Z||000000||maryjane||11-20-2001||02:18 AM||||Got this off another forum, well sort of.<BR>The FBI is stymied and asking for help. Originally said it would be solved by someone bragging or something from a friend.. The guy who posted this question says he will post the answer to this clue in a day or two, thought I would throw it out to you guys/girls. He said it is a clue/evidence the FBI is overlooking.<BR>All the 'infected' envelopes were pretty much the same. But the question:<BR> <BR>"Why would you buy a pre-stamped, undersized (6.75" envelope for $.42 when you could buy a reg stamp for $.34 and use a regular business envelope that is so common, or if you just happened to like little envelopes, use the std 6.75" envelope and buy the cheaper $.34 stamp for it?"<P>Any guesses? I'll post back when he posts his answer. I personally thought it might have to do with not leaving any DNA in the act of attaching the stamp, but you could use a peel off stamp or a moist towel to do it. <BR>Don<P><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 11-20-2001).]||||reg||1
