Z||000009||Raydar||11-20-2001||10:44 AM||||True story. <BR>Happened at a friend's workplace.<BR>Seems that their secretary was sorting the mail, wearing latex gloves. <BR>He told her, "Don't worry. Anthrax has a very distinctive odor."<BR>She said, "Really?" ...and proceed to hold an envelope to her nose and take a big whiff.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>As for the clue... <BR>Don't non-standard envelopes have to be sorted by hand? Thereby adding a bunch of different fingerprints and body oils to the mix?<BR>I <I>don't</I> think it was done in order to infect the postal workers. Just think it was a side effect.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||11-20-2001||10:55 AM||||just the opposite - the anthrax envelope they found recently was leaking anthrax - so whoever mailed it must have been wearing protection and gloves, or he is dead now<P> so I doubt he was worried about his own fingerprints being on the envelope.<BR> <BR> but I suspect if he knew that odd sized envelopes have to be hand sorted - that WOULD be his motivation - they are out to murder people at random - the more the better.<P> BTW I wonder if these were mailed by one of the terrorist on one of the planes? Maybe they knew they would be dead in a few days anyway.||||reg||11
